{
  "name": "Call interested prospects: get their phone number and post a call task to Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Call interested prospects: get their phone number and post a call task to Slack\n\n### How it works\nStrike while the reply is warm. When a reply is labeled Interested or Meeting request, the workflow looks up the person behind the email in Argorant, then asks for their direct or mobile number. With a number, Slack gets a call task: name, title, company, a tel: link and the first lines of the reply. Without one, Slack gets a short note to answer by email instead. Phone numbers come with the Pro plan.\n\nCosts: 10 credits per number returned, free when none is found or you already have it; the person lookup costs 1 credit per match.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Activate the trigger with your Argorant credential. Argorant webhooks come with the Pro plan, and your n8n needs a public HTTPS address.\n4. Add a Slack credential and pick the channel in both Slack nodes.\n\n### Customization\nCreate a task in your CRM instead of a Slack message, or call only for one campaign with the trigger's Campaign option.",
        "height": 636,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
